      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "What you should suggest is how you would have this adjustment.\n\nHowever!  I can supply a suggestion!\n\nAs of right now, animations are based around the height of the character, from the ground up.  If chairs could be ties to the hips/pelvis bone, it could allow better compensation, but... even that would has some complications.  It would have to be a specialized format, and would be difficult to adapt for every avatar.  \n\nIf there is a way to lock to a specific named Bone, like \"seat bone\" that uploaders could incorperate, so that when seating the offset could be made on creation for that specific sitting animation.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-10-24T20:35:36.510Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, when an avatar is shorter than that of 4 or so feet (I've done testing, but none of the results would say an exact cutting off point, but it seems to start happening at around 4 feet) if that avatar were to sit in a chair, the avatar would appear to be sitting inside of the chair, It'd be nice if there could be a way to re-compensate a lot of stuff for smaller avatars",
